# Supply-chain gate. Refuse any package version published more recently than this,
# because a compromised maintainer account shows up as a brand-new release and the
# window in which nobody has looked at it yet is the whole of the exposure.
#
# The unit is DAYS, as a plain integer, and that is the one thing in this file that
# has to be right. npm rejects a duration string like `2d`, and it fails *open* on a
# value it cannot parse - a warning rather than an error - so a wrong unit reads as a
# configured gate while blocking nothing. Other package managers in this family take
# minutes or seconds, which is exactly how the wrong number gets written here.
#
# Verify what npm derived rather than reading this line back: `npm config get before`
# must answer a date about two days in the past. Asking for `min-release-age` is not a
# check - it always reads back null, whether it took effect or not.
min-release-age=2
